791.description:
Better, more dynamic, more interesting! That's exactly what the developers were aiming for when creating the new Half-Life 2: Cinematic Mod. Particular attention was paid to the graphics, with stunning animation effects.

Game features:
- Alix. The Alix model was based on Jamil Mullen, but a model based on Adriana Lima is also available. Each model emphasizes the eyes, recreating a wetness effect and reflecting everything she sees.
- High-quality facial animation allows the characters to look as realistic as possible, just like in life.
- Two episodes with the FakeFactory modification. Half-Life 2 invites you to take part in the adventures of Gordon Freeman, a brilliant scientist who has dedicated his life to exploring and fighting aliens who invade the human world. His new journey brings him into contact with Combine military equipment, aliens, and enhanced humans (who act as obedient servants of the invaders). Gordon convinces the population to rise up against the invaders and end their oppression.
In the first episode - Half-Life 2: Episode One, the storyline continues Freeman's story, where he teams up with Alyx and her robot Dog to throw everything they have into helping the rebels defeat the Combine.
The second episode takes things more dynamically, offering the player the chance to re-enter the world of Alyx and Freeman and continue their adventure – finding themselves in the White Forest and experiencing the full scope of a combat vehicle battle, and much more…

Repack features:
- The mod has been updated to the latest version at the time of the project freezing - 1,24;
- There are two voice acting options to choose from - the corrected one from VALVE and from BUKA;
- Partially non-working launcher has been replaced with our own;
- Nothing has been cut or re-encoded (original sound);
- More than 140 Alix models;
- There are two types of soundtrack - the original and from the creators of the mod (pretty good, but loud);
- Installation time - 10 minutes on different physical HDDs
